text: ['Altar of the Lost enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add two mana in any combination of colors. Spend this mana only to cast spells with flashback from a graveyard.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nHeadless Skaab enters the battlefield tapped.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nFling deals damage equal to the sacrificed creature's power to any target.", 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Afflicted Deserter.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Hinterland Hermit.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Lambholt Elder.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Mondronen Shaman.', "At the beginning of each upkeep, you may exile target creature card from your graveyard. If you do, create a token that's a copy of that card, except it's a Spirit in addition to its other types. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.", "At the beginning of your end step, you may sacrifice a nontoken creature. If you do, create X 2/2 green Wolf creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's toughness.", 'Burning Oil deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.\\nFlashback {3}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Choose one —\\n• Destroy target creature with flying.\\n• Destroy target artifact.', 'Copy target instant or sorcery spell you control. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, copy that spell twice instead. You may choose new targets for the copies.\\nFlashback {3}{R}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Counter target creature spell.\\nDraw a card.', 'Counter target spell. You may cast a spell that shares a card type with it from your hand without paying its mana cost.', 'Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nFlashback {4}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Create five 1/1 white Human creature tokens. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, create ten of those tokens instead.\\nFlashback {7}{W}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Create two 1/1 white Human creature tokens.\\nFateful hour — If you have 5 or less life, create five of those tokens instead.', 'Create two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying.\\nFlashback {1}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Creature cards in graveyards and libraries can't enter the battlefield.\\nPlayers can't cast spells from graveyards or libraries.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+4 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nFateful hour — If you have 5 or less life, those creatures gain indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them.)', 'Deathtouch\\nOther Zombie creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever another Zombie you control dies, target opponent loses 1 life.', 'Destroy target creature. If that creature was a Human, you gain life equal to its toughness.', 'Destroy target enchantment.\\nFlashback {G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Destroy target land. Scorch the Fields deals 1 damage to each Human creature.', 'Discard all the cards in your hand, then draw that many cards.\\nFlashback {5}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Double strike\\nWhenever Markov Blademaster deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Draw a card for each creature card in your graveyard.', 'Draw two cards, then discard two cards.\\nFlashback {2}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Draw two cards.', 'Each player mills five cards.\\nFlashback {7}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may look at the top five cards of your library. If you do, you may put a creature card that shares a creature type with enchanted creature from among them onto the battlefield, then you put the rest of those cards on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -13/-0.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature blocks, you gain 3 life.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to its controller.', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\n{1}: Tap enchanted creature.', "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of enchanted player's upkeep, Curse of Thirst deals damage to that player equal to the number of Curses attached to them.", "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may search your library for a Curse card that doesn't have the same name as a Curse attached to enchanted player, put it onto the battlefield attached to that player, then shuffle.", "Enchant player\\nEnchanted player can't cast more than one spell each turn.", 'Enchant player\\nIf a source would deal damage to enchanted player, it deals double that damage to that player instead.', 'Enchant player\\nWhenever enchanted player casts an instant or sorcery spell, each other player may copy that spell and may choose new targets for the copy they control.', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0 and has vigilance.\\nWhenever equipped creature dies, if it was a Human, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0.\\nWhen equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, unattach Elbrus, the Binding Blade, then transform it.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+1.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it gets an additional +1/+1.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature has "{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target" and "{T}: This creature deals 3 damage to target Werewolf creature."\\nEquip {5}', "Equipped creature has intimidate. (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", "Exile all nonland permanents target player controls. Return the exiled cards to the battlefield under their owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Fateful hour — As long as you have 5 or less life, other creatures you control get +1/+4.', 'Fires of Undeath deals 2 damage to any target.\\nFlashback {5}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'First strike\\nNoncreature spells cost {1} more to cast.', 'First strike\\nOther Vampire creatures you control get +1/+1 and have first strike.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{1}{R}: This creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn."', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Hollowhenge Spirit enters the battlefield, remove target attacking or blocking creature from combat.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Briarpack Alpha enters the battlefield, target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying, double strike, lifelink\\nWhenever you gain life, draw a card.', 'Flying, first strike', 'Flying, haste\\nSacrifice a creature: Falkenrath Aristocrat gains indestructible until end of turn. If the sacrificed creature was a Human, put a +1/+1 counter on Falkenrath Aristocrat.', "Flying, intimidate, trample (A creature with intimidate can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nWhenever a player loses the game, put thirteen +1/+1 counters on Withengar Unbound.", "Flying, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a Human. If you can't, tap Archdemon of Greed and it deals 9 damage to you.", "Flying\\nOther Spirit creatures you control get +1/+1 and have hexproof. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Flying\\nStormbound Geist can block only creatures with flying.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Flying\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Flying\\nWhen Dungeon Geists enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as you control Dungeon Geists.", 'Flying\\nWhen Niblis of the Mist enters the battlefield, you may tap target creature.', 'Flying\\nWhen Soul Seizer deals combat damage to a player, you may transform it. If you do, attach it to target creature that player controls.', 'Flying\\nWhen Tower Geist enters the battlefield, look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other into your graveyard.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Fiend of the Shadows deals combat damage to a player, that player exiles a card from their hand. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled.\\nSacrifice a Human: Regenerate Fiend of the Shadows.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Niblis of the Urn attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Shriekgeist deals combat damage to a player, that player mills two cards.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another non-Spirit creature you control dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Each creature you control gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", "Geralf's Messenger enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Geralf's Messenger enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 2 life.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Gravecrawler can't block.\\nYou may cast Gravecrawler from your graveyard as long as you control a Zombie.", "Haste\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Haste\\nWhen Markov Warlord enters the battlefield, up to two target creatures can't block this turn.", 'Haste\\nWhenever Erdwal Ripper deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Haste\\nWhenever a creature you control attacks, Hellrider deals 1 damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.", 'Hinterland Scourge must be blocked if able.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Hinterland Scourge.', 'Indestructible\\nWhenever Predator Ooze attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Predator Ooze this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Predator Ooze.', "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nEach other creature you control that's a Wolf or a Werewolf gets +1/+1.\\nNon-Human Werewolves you control can't transform.", "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nWhenever a Human deals damage to you, destroy it.\\nOther non-Human creatures you control get +1/+1 and have undying. (When a creature with undying dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nWhen Elgaud Inquisitor dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Morbid — When Ulvenwald Bear enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.', 'Morbid — When Wakedancer enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', "Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.\\nFateful hour — If you have 5 or less life, tap all attacking creatures. Those creatures don't untap during their controller's next untap step.", 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nMorbid — Put three +1/+1 counters on that creature instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Put any number of target creature cards from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDraw a card.', 'Put five +1/+1 counters on target creature. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, put ten +1/+1 counters on that creature instead.\\nFlashback {5}{G}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nDeathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Return all Zombie creature cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped, then destroy all Humans.', 'Return target creature you own to your hand.\\nFlashback {W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.\\nFlashback {2}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Reveal the top four cards of your library. Put a creature card from among them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nFlashback {2}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Sacrifice a Human: Transform Ravenous Demon. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Falkenrath Torturer gains flying until end of turn. If the sacrificed creature was a Human, put a +1/+1 counter on Falkenrath Torturer.', 'Search your library for a card and put that card into your hand. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, instead search your library for two cards and put those cards into your hand. Then shuffle.\\nFlashback {7}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Sightless Ghoul can't block.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Target creature an opponent controls deals damage equal to its power to each other creature that player controls, then each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power to that creature.', "Target creature can't be blocked this turn.\\nFlashback {U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Target creature deals damage to itself equal to its power.', 'Target creature fights another target creature. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', 'Target creature gains deathtouch until end of turn and must be blocked this turn if able.\\nFlashback {G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Target creature gains undying until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.\\nFlashback {3}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nMorbid — That creature gets -13/-13 until end of turn instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Target permanent you control gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.\\nFateful hour — If you have 5 or less life, instead you and each permanent you control gain protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Target player discards two cards.\\nMorbid — If a creature died this turn, instead that player reveals their hand, you choose two cards from it, then that player discards those cards.', 'Target player draws three cards and loses 3 life.', 'Target player mills X cards. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, that player mills twice that many cards instead.\\nFlashback {X}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target player mills two cards.\\nDraw a card.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature card in your graveyard.', 'Trample\\nMorbid — Gravetiller Wurm enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it if a creature died this turn.', "Trample\\nWhenever this creature transforms into Ravager of the Fells, it deals 2 damage to target opponent or planeswalker and 2 damage to up to one target creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Ravager of the Fells.", "Undying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Undying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever Flayer of the Hatebound or another creature enters the battlefield from your graveyard, that creature deals damage equal to its power to any target.", "Unhallowed Cathar can't block.", "Vigilance, trample\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Vigilance\\nFateful hour — As long as you have 5 or less life, other creatures you control have vigilance.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Loyal Cathar dies, return it to the battlefield transformed under your control at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Vigilance\\n{T}: Add {G}{G}.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Moonscarred Werewolf.', "Warden of the Wall enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\nAs long as it's not your turn, Warden of the Wall is a 2/3 Gargoyle artifact creature with flying.", 'When Black Cat dies, target opponent discards a card at random.', 'When Farbog Boneflinger enters the battlefield, target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'When Forge Devil enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to target creature and 1 damage to you.', "When Geralf's Mindcrusher enters the battlefield, target player mills five cards.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'When Screeching Skaab enters the battlefield, mill two cards.', "Whenever Pyreheart Wolf attacks, creatures you control gain menace until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Whenever Silverpelt Werewolf deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Silverpelt Werewolf.', "Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a Forest card, remove that creature from combat. Then put the revealed card on the bottom of your library.", 'Whenever a creature you control dies, put two eyeball counters on Jar of Eyeballs.\\n{3}, {T}, Remove all eyeball counters from Jar of Eyeballs: Look at the top X cards of your library, where X is the number of eyeball counters removed this way. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Whenever an opponent casts a spell, Tovolar's Magehunter deals 2 damage to that player.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Tovolar's Magehunter.", 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, untap Midnight Guard.', 'Whenever this creature enters the battlefield or transforms into Huntmaster of the Fells, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token and you gain 2 life.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Huntmaster of the Fells.', "Whenever this creature transforms into Werewolf Ransacker, you may destroy target artifact. If that artifact is put into a graveyard this way, Werewolf Ransacker deals 3 damage to that artifact's controller.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Werewolf Ransacker.", 'Whenever you cast a spell from your graveyard, draw a card.', 'You gain 2 life for each card in your graveyard, then shuffle your graveyard into your library.', '[+1]: Create a 1/1 black Vampire creature token with lifelink.\\n[−2]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +1/+0."\\n[−6]: Destroy up to three target creatures and/or other planeswalkers. Return each card put into a graveyard this way to the battlefield under your control.', "{1}, {T}: Exile target creature you control.\\n{7}, {T}: Exile target creature you don't control.\\nWhen Helvault is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return all cards exiled with it to the battlefield under their owners' control.", '{1}: You may cast target creature card in a graveyard this turn. When you cast it this turn, Havengul Lich gains all activated abilities of that card until end of turn.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice a Human: Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.', '{1}{G}: Wolfbitten Captive gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Wolfbitten Captive.', '{2}{R}: Target creature attacks this turn if able.', '{2}{U}, {T}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token, then put a +1/+1 counter on each Zombie creature you control.', '{3}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a Human: Destroy target creature.', '{3}{G}: Krallenhorde Killer gets +4/+4 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Krallenhorde Killer.', '{G}, Sacrifice Dawntreader Elk: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{R}, Sacrifice Torch Fiend: Destroy target artifact.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Tap an untapped Vampire you control: Transform Chosen of Markov.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{B}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{W}{B}, {T}: Creatures you control gain deathtouch and lifelink until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Haunted Fengraf: Return a creature card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Scorned Villager.', '{T}: Create a 1/1 white Human creature token.\\nFateful hour — As long as you have 5 or less life, other creatures you control get +2/+2.', '{T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard.', '{T}: Gain control of target creature with power less than or equal to the number of creatures you control.', '{T}: Target player loses 5 life.', '{T}: You gain 1 life. Then if you have at least 10 life more than your starting life total, transform Chalice of Life.']
flavor: ['". . . and I will bring the fury of the wild back to my village."', '". . . and for that I shall be eternally grateful."', '"All the dead sleep lightly here, no matter how refined their beds may be."\\n—Grafdigger Wulmer', '"As you inject the *viscus vitae* into the brain stem, don\'t let the spastic moaning bother you. It will soon become music to your ears."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Avacyn has abandoned us! We have nothing left except what we can take!"', '"Be wary of the seemingly gentle souls. The weak here were slaughtered long ago."\\n—Rem Karolus, Blade of the Inquisitors', '"Behind every devil\'s mayhem lurks a demon\'s scheme."\\n—Rem Karolus, Blade of the Inquisitors', '"Beware the seagrafs just off the shore. These waters are filled with hungry geists looking for an easy meal."\\n—Captain Eberhart', '"Come, let me free you of the tyranny of thought."', '"Do not speak of this to the elders. They look unfavorably upon my indulgences."', '"For centuries my creation kept this world in balance. Now only her shadow remains."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"Grab an axe and defend the gate! Your despair is an extravagance we can ill afford."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Here are some bones for you to choke on, dear brother!"\\n—Gisa, to Geralf', '"I can think of worse ways to go. On second thought, maybe not."\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"I do believe your heresy will prove more difficult now that you have more pressing concerns."\\n—Bishop Argust', '"I drink of those who are worthy of my palate. The rest I burn."', '"I have been found worthy by this great house . . ."', '"I love what they\'ve done with the place."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"I never had the nerve to open that bottle. I\'ll bet you\'re wishing right now you hadn\'t been so curious yourself."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"I trust myself to do my duty, even unto death. It\'s what comes after that I\'m afraid of."\\n—Constable Visil, to Thalia', '"I wish my work could shelter everyone, yet I pray we are never so few that it does."', '"If you think you\'ve killed one, guess again."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"If you wind up in one of mine, you can be sure as silver it will be your last."\\n—Grafdigger Wulmer', '"Innistrad\'s ghoulcallers are talented enough, but let me show you what someone with real power can create."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Is it true the evil that people do follows them into death? Let\'s find out."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"It may not look like much, but it\'s a good old door with strong wards. It\'ll hold."\\n—Olgard of the Skiltfolk', '"It will take more than steel alone to purge this world of evil."', '"Just fight without fear. Your soul is protected by the hand of Avacyn and will never submit to evil."\\n—Thalia, to Constable Visil', '"Keep one eye on the cliff road or you may fall to your death. Keep one eye on the sky or your death may fall on you."\\n—Manfried Ulmach, Elgaud Master-at-Arms', '"Let them decry me for burning the dead. I\'m not giving those ghoulcallers any more fuel for their madness."', '"Let us remind these human cattle why they fear the shadows of this world."\\n—Aldreg, Skirsdag cultist', '"May angels carry him into the Blessed Sleep with dreams of sunlit days and moonless nights."\\n—Tomb inscription of Saint Raban', '"May you drink until you drown but never be sated."\\n—Odila, witch of Morkrut', '"Mortals practice swordplay for a few decades at best. How can they ever attain the exquisite mastery that eternity has to offer?"', '"My village\'s fear drove me into the wild . . ."', '"No longer can we allow our human populations to be mindlessly slaughtered by ghouls. Slay all who trespass."\\n—Runo Stromkirk', '"Not even a roaring fire could thaw the chill it put in my heart."\\n—Vonn, geist-trapper', '"Nothing in nature goes to waste, not even the rotting corpse of a good-for-nothing, blood-sucking vampire."\\n—Halana of Ulvenwald', '"Our world is vast, but Thraben is its heart. The cathedral must stand even if the hinterlands are lost."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Pathetic. Let me show you how it\'s done."', '"So many corpses, so little time."', '"Steel in the heart, silver in the bow."\\n—Wolfhunter\'s creed', '"Swarms of the unhallowed claw at Thraben\'s gates! Do you still deny the end approaches?"', '"The Blessed Sleep? Ha! Wake up my lovelies, there\'s work to be done!"\\n—Gisa, ghoulcaller of Gavony', '"The price is paid. The power is mine!"', '"The veil between the living and the dead is so very thin that the whispers of the ancients can finally be heard."\\n—Amalric of Midvast Hall', '"The wolves of our valley are bred to detest the scent of ghouls. For centuries they have kept our estates clear of such carrion."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"The wolves turned on us and a chill swept over me. The pack had a new leader."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"Their hearts beat, their lungs draw breath, and they have one true form. I count them as allies of the living."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"There are always fools who attempt to traverse Kruin Pass before sundown and every time they wind up in a race for their lives."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"There was a time when our cages rang with wailing. Now only a handful of these whimpering fools remain."', '"There will come a day so dark you will pray for death. On that day your prayers will be answered."\\n—Minaldra, the Vizag Atum', '"This is the light of Avacyn. Even in her absence she offers us hope."\\n—Radulf, priest of Avacyn', '"Thraben is our home and I will not see it fall to this unhallowed horde."', '"Tovolar, my master. Gather the howlpack, for the Hunter\'s Moon is nigh and Thraben\'s walls grow weak."', '"Valor is a currency of the living that serves us well."\\n—Cosper Lowe of the Silbern Guard', '"Wait . . . did you fellows hear something?"', '"Werewolves are an unholy mix of a predator\'s instinct and a human\'s hatred."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"What use is a stake or holy symbol in the hands of a coward?"', '"When you\'re on watch, no noise is harmless and no shadow can be ignored."\\n—Olgard of the Skiltfolk', '"Why do the dead remain among us? Where is Flight Alabaster to lead them home? Where is Avacyn?"\\n—Eruth of Lambholt', '"You must shatter the fetters of the past. Only then can you truly act."\\n—Rem Karolus, Blade of the Inquisitors', '"Your blood is quite pleasing. A pity there\'s not enough for both of us."', '"Your fields will turn as black as a ghoul\'s tongue and fire shall be your only harvest."\\n—Minaldra, the Vizag Atum', '"Your veil\'s curse won\'t stop me, deathmage. I have taken down countless night hunters and this dark plane is not big enough for you to hide."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker, to Liliana Vess', '. . . but the monster within was a tireless hunter.', "A ghoulcaller's playground.", "A head is a needless encumbrance when muscle is all that's required.", "As the creatures of the night closed in on humanity, Innistrad's primeval forces stirred, as though waking to watch the slaughter.", 'As their villages fell to werewolves, fleeing refugees discovered they too had remarkable survival instincts.', 'Being an alpha means proving it every full moon.', 'Cast out by his village, he now takes grim offense at refugees who seek shelter in his forest.', "Cats prowl the corridors of Avacyn's churches in search of devils or signs of their mischief.", 'Certain initiates into the Skirsdag cult take a vow of blindness, pledging obedience to none but demonkind.', 'Dead or alive, true leaders can inspire an entire army.', 'Devils infiltrated the lower levels of Thraben Cathedral, making cracks in load-bearing pillars and setting fire to precious archives.', 'Devils redecorate every room with fire.', "Even the House of Galan, who takes the most scholarly approach to the mystic traditions, has resorted to exploring more primitive methods in Avacyn's absence.", "Every now and then, a devil's prank can give you a good idea.", 'Feeling abandoned by Avacyn, some Kessigers turned to the pagan rituals of their ancestors.', 'Fusing intelligence with the power of undeath requires inspiration of the darkest kind.', 'Geists of the hanged often haunt the tree on which they died.', 'He tried to live far from those he could hurt . . .', 'He wields the full power of wrath unfettered by the sympathies of a soul.', 'Hers is an ancient form of necromancy, steeped in shamanic trance and ritual that few skaberen or ghoulcallers comprehend.', 'His twisted words entice the weak.', "In a world of monsters, it's the stuff of nightmares.", 'In the memories of those they lost lies the strength needed to defend their city.', "It blindly marches on Thraben's gates, guided by its master's direful will.", "It is the demon's mark, an infernal claim on the flesh of the guilty.", 'It patrols the grafs for miles around Thraben, ensuring that the unhallowed do not wake for long.', 'It uproots entire fengrafs to add to its twisted frame.', 'Its last life is spent tormenting your dreams.', 'Its screeching is the sound of you losing your mind.', 'Its silk is highly prized, but then again, so is your life.', "Jenrik's tower is served by those who once sought to enter it uninvited.", "Linger on death's door and risk being invited in.", 'Masters of the sword know the blade is not the only weapon at their disposal.', "Nothing's more valuable than perfect timing.", 'Otto the Hunter was filled with many grand ambitions. The snake was filled only with Otto.', 'Out chasing bears\\n—Kessig expression meaning "died in the woods"', "Savage vampires lurk in the Erdwal's network of passageways where prey is plentiful and easy to catch.", 'Silent as winter snow, it seeks wild places unspoiled by the walking dead.', 'Some spirits mourn. Others terrorize.', 'Succession is a matter of blood, and by blood it is often decided.', 'The Somberwald is her domain, and she has yet to hear an acceptable excuse for trespassing.', "The Ulvenwald makes no allowances for youth. Today's newborn is either tomorrow's hunter or tomorrow's lunch.", "The bitter taste of life's only certainty.", 'The body often twists and flails spasmodically as the spirit explores its new home.', 'The faint smell of cloves, the rustling of the wind, and a paralyzing descent into an airless, fathomless tomb.', 'The murdered inhabitants of Hollowhenge impart to the living the terror they felt in death.', 'The rising of the first full moon eliminated any doubt as to the horrible truth lurking within.', 'The skathul, spirits consumed by revenge, fester and seethe while looking for weak minds to assault.', 'The skifsang, seafarers of Nephalia, craft spells like other sailors craft nets—making them strong enough to snare even the deadliest catch.', "The sweet taste of hope's promise.", 'The wreck hung on the jagged reef, each night disgorging more of its gruesome cargo.', 'Their language may be a cacophonous agglomeration of chittering snorts and mad barking, but the message they send is all too clear.', 'There are not enough lives on Innistrad to satisfy his thirst for retribution.', "Those who grasp its hilt soon hear the demon's call.", 'Those who know the alleys and sewers of the Erdwal can disappear like smoke.', 'Though its mind has long since rotted away, it wields a sword with deadly skill.', 'What could be more irresistible than death?', 'When angels despair, what hope can remain for mortals?', 'Wounds of the flesh are easy to heal. Wounds of the mind may never be undone.', 'Wracked and warped with anguish, it obsessively seeks out other souls to hoard within its eternal prison.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Austin Hsu', 'Bud Cook', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eytan Zana', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Stanko', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Michael Komarck', 'Mike Sass', 'Nils Hamm', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Scott Chou', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne England', 'Winona Nelson', 'Zoltan Boros']
